<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Seraikela State</h1><p class="st-meta">1620 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Seraikela</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Singh Deo-ruled state of the Chota Nagpur plateau, cradle of the masked Seraikela style of Chhau dance.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Seraikela was founded around 1620 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bikram-singh-of-seraikela">Bikram Singh</a>, a member of the Singh Deo family of Porahat, who carved out his own principality on the Kharkai river. The neighbouring state of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kharsawan-state">Kharsawan</a> later branched from the same family.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rajas ruled a population of Ho, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santal-people">Santal</a> and Oriya-speaking peasants. From 1820 the state came under British protection and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-states-agency">Eastern States Agency</a>. The court patronised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhau-dance">Chhau dance</a>, whose Seraikela form uses distinctive painted masks.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Seraikela was briefly merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> in January 1948 but was transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> later that year after local opposition. It is now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seraikela-kharsawan-district">Seraikela Kharsawan district</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jharkhand">Jharkhand</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/seraikela-state.jpg" alt="Seraikela State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Saraikela_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1620 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Seraikela</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bikram Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia, Ho</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Saraikela</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1784&amp;focus=seraikela-state" aria-label="Seraikela State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6979 1340 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Seraikela State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7299 1596L7364 1601M7299 1596L7364 1602M7299 1596L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7299 1596h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7299 1596h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1784&amp;focus=seraikela-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
